hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1683","Narrated to us Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la: Narrated to us Ibn Wahb: Narrated to us 'Amr ibn al-Harith: That Darraj Abu al-Samh informed him, from al-Sa'ib, the freed slave of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said:\n\n\The best mosques for women are the inner parts of their houses.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"1684","**\nNarrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad Az-Za'farani, who said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us.\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Rafi', who said: Yazid narrated to us, who said: Al-'Awwam ibn Hawshab narrated to us, who said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n*\Do not prevent your women from going to the mosques"","" but their homes are better for them.\""*\n\nA son of 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (RA) said: \""Nay"","" by Allah"","" we will indeed prevent them.\""\nSo Ibn 'Umar (RA) said: \""Do you hear me narrating from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and then say what you say?!\""\n\nBoth narrations are identical in wording.\n\nAnd narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad"","" who said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf Al-Azraq narrated to us"","" who said: Al-'Awwam narrated to us with this chain in a similar manner."""""
"1685","###\n Abu Musa narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, who said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Mawarriq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Indeed"","" the woman is a 'awrah (something to be covered/protected); when she goes out"","" Satan seeks to attract attention to her. And the closest she is to the Face of her Lord is when"""""
"1686","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam who said: Al-Mu'tamir informed us, he said: I heard my father narrating, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he said:\n\The woman is 'awrah (a thing to be concealed)"","" and when she goes out"","" the Shaytan seeks to tempt her. Verily"","" she does not draw closer to Allah in any position than when she is in the depths of her house.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"1687","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya; narrated to us Muhammad ibn Uthman, known as the Damascene; he narrated to us Sa'd ibn Bashir; on the authority of Qatada; on the authority of Murriq; on the authority of Abi al-Ahwas; on the authority of Abdullah. It is reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said [the same ruling as the topic of this chapter, i.e., that a woman’s prayer in her home is more virtuous than her prayer in the mosque]. Abu Bakr [the hadith critic] stated: \I only rejected this report because I question whether Qatada actually heard this narration from Abi al-Ahwas"","" as Sulaiman al-Ta’imi has narrated this same report from Qatada directly from Abi al-Ahwas"","" having omitted Murriq from the chain of narration. Hammam and Sa'id ibn Bashir"","" by contrast"","" included Murriq in their chains. I also doubt the authenticity of this hadith because I have no confirmed record of Qatada hearing this report from Murriq.\"""""""
